35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The survey caps the bay at four hundred kilos per square metre. That’s a hard limit we can’t ignore.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The maintenance log confirms seventeen call-outs, four during opening hours. The bay is already under strain.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,The lab is down to one person with two hundred pieces waiting. We simply cannot process new loans.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Two openings slipped because paperwork arrived after the shipping cut-off. We keep promising what we can’t deliver on time.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Transport and crating ate a third of the installation budget. The joiner’s rate has also doubled, so bespoke mounts are now a luxury we can’t afford.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, with the bay already strained and capped, we must avoid any proposal requiring heavy overhead rigging.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, agreed. The log proves the bay is already failing under current loads.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, if bespoke mounts are too expensive, we must choose objects that arrive ready to display, or we’ll be stuck.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that third of the budget on transport is exactly why the paperwork delays hurt so much.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, precisely. The delays force expensive emergency crating, which is why the transport line item swallows the rest.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, the lab backlog means we cannot rely on on-site conservation. We need a proposal that doesn’t require stabilizing fragile finds.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, correct. We must avoid anything requiring active conservation work. The lab is simply not equipped to handle it.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, agreed. The volunteer roster is mostly the town history circle, so we need a show they can actually guide without extra training.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, the town history circle fits perfectly with local weaving and regional crafts. They already know that material.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that’s a good point, but I need to see if the transport costs for local items are actually lower than the loans.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, local items avoid the shipping cut-offs entirely. That solves the delivery problem before it starts.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, the head counts will confirm if that local appeal actually draws the crowds we need.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, exactly. The town history circle knows the old quarter, so they can guide the local crafts without extra training.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, the head counts show crowds climb where mechanisms run, but drop in static rooms. Local crafts need live demos to hold them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, live demonstrations solve the crowd problem, but I need to confirm the local sourcing keeps the transport line item from swallowing the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
