60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The candidates are here. Given the bay’s weight limit and the lab’s backlog, I’m worried about anything heavy or fragile.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, agreed. The structural and conservation constraints rule out heavy stonework or fragile finds immediately.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, the town history circle fits perfectly with local weaving. They already know that material, so we avoid extra training.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, exactly. Local weaving means no distant lenders, so no shipping cut-offs to trip us up.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, local sourcing eliminates the transport and crating costs that have been eating our budget. It’s the only option that fits the finances.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the structural survey confirms the bay cannot support the overhead rigging required for the light and motion proposal.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, correct. The rigging exceeds the cap. We must reject that option to protect the building.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the local weaving fits the finances, but I need to ensure the volunteer roster can actually handle the demonstration sessions without burning out.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, the town history circle already guides the old quarter, so they know the local context. They can handle the demos without extra training.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the local sourcing keeps the budget safe, but I need to confirm the demonstration sessions don’t require expensive specialist equipment.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the maintenance log shows powered displays cause failures. Textiles are static, so they won’t strain the bay or trigger call-outs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, precisely. Static textiles eliminate the maintenance risk entirely. The record shows crowds return for presence, not mechanisms, so this fits the data.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, the town history circle knows the local context, so they can handle the demos without extra training.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, agreed. The circle’s familiarity with the region means they can lead the interviews and demonstrations without the training costs we can’t afford.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the demonstrations use existing tools, so no new equipment costs. The budget stays intact, and the local sourcing keeps transport near zero.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I’m ready to vote. Textiles of the Region is the only candidate that respects the bay’s limits and our staffing reality.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, agreed. The record confirms presence drives return visits, and textiles provide that without the structural or conservation risks. I vote for Textiles of the Region.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I’m ready. The circle can handle the demos, and the lab stays clear. I vote for Textiles of the Region.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the local sourcing means no distant lenders, so no shipping cut-offs to trip us up. I vote for Textiles of the Region.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the numbers confirm it. No transport, no bespoke mounts, no emergency crating. The budget finally stays where it belongs. I vote for Textiles of the Region.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
